### HTTP retry classification

Use the existing `ApiError.retryable` contract (`api.ts:100`), which already marks 429 (and 5xx) retryable — do NOT hand-roll a `status >= 500` check that would wrongly make 429 terminal (Finding 5).

```typescript
function isRetryable(err: unknown): boolean {
  if (err instanceof TypeError) return true;                 // fetch network error, no status
  if (err instanceof ApiError) return err.retryable;         // honors 429 + 5xx per api.ts:100
  return false;
}
function isLegacyAmbiguous(err: unknown): boolean {
  return err instanceof ApiError && err.status === 409
    && errorCodeOf(err) === 'LEGACY_AMBIGUOUS';
}
// classification: network error | ApiError.retryable (incl. 429) → awaiting_http_retry;
//                 LEGACY_AMBIGUOUS → succeeded; all other 4xx (incl. IDEMPOTENCY_CONFLICT) → terminal_error
```

`scheduleHttpRetry`: backoff `min(2^attempts, 60)s`, **honoring `Retry-After` when present** (use `max(backoff, retryAfterMs)`); sets `awaiting_http_retry`, timer → `pending` → drain. `drainOutbox` skips `awaiting_http_retry`. `awaiting_http_retry` survives all resets. `dispose()` cancels all timers.

